==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{af|la|tam||alt2=-em}}. Last particle in {{m|la|īdem}}. Compare with its later doublet: {{m|la|tandem}}. Both with original meaning supposedly ''"so(much)ever"''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA}}
* Note: unlike in {{m|la|tametsī}}, the graphic ''m'' does represent the bilabial nasal /m/.

===Conjunction===
{{head|la|conjunction}}

# {{lb|la|usually|postpositive}} [[in spite of]] what has been said, [[nevertheless]], [[however]], [[notwithstanding]]
#: {{Q|la|Terence|Andria|864|quote=''SIMO'' Nihil audiō! Ego iam tē commōtum reddam! ''DAVUS'' Tamen etsī hoc vērum·st? ''SIM'' '''Tamen!'''|t=''SI'' I'm not listening! I'm gonna pull at your heart strings real good now! ''DA'' Even if it's true? ''SI'' Even so!}}
# {{q|expressing a concession}} [[nevertheless]], [[yet]], [[still]]
# [[just the same]] {{gl|in spite of evidence to the contrary}}
#: {{uxi|la|ac '''tamen'''...|and '''yet'''...}}
# {{q|in an aside}} [[although]]
# {{q|in a limiting clause}} {{lb|la|also|with|[[ut]]|or|[[ne]]}} [[at least]]

